r (GCD) of two numbers along with the coefficients (a and b) such that\n62\t * gcd = ax + by.\n63\t *\n64\t * @param a The first number.\n65\t * @param b The second number.\n66\t *\n67\t * @return The extended greatest common divisor (xgcd) result.\n68\t */\n69\tXgcd xgcd(uint64_t a, uint64_t b);\n70\t\n71\t/**\n72\t * @brief Check if two numbers are coprime.\n73\t *\n74\t * This function checks if two unsigned 64-bit integers are coprime,\n75\t * meaning their greatest common divisor (GCD) is equal to 1.\n76\t *\n77\t * @param x The first number.\n78\t * @param y The second number.\n79\t *\n80\t * @return 1 if the numbers are coprime, 0 otherwise.\n81\t */\n82\tint are_coprime(uint64_t x, uint64_t y);\n83\t\n84\t/**\n85\t * @brief Generate a random pair of inverses.\n86\t *\n87\t * This function generates a random pair of inverses for a given value.\n88\t * It selects a random number 'a' within the range [2, value - 1], ensuring\n89\t * that 'a' is coprime with the given value. Then, it computes the modular\n90\t * inverse of 'a' with respect to the given value and returns a pair consisting\n91\t * of 'a' and its modular inverse.\n92\t *\n93\t * @param value The value for which inverses are generated.\n94\t *\n95\t * @return A pair containing 'a' and its modular inverse.\n96\t */\n97\tPair randinverse(uint64_t value);\n98\t\n99\t/**\n100\t * @brief Generate a random number within a specified range.\n101\t *\n102\t * This function generates a random unsigned 64-bit integer within the specified\n103\t * range [lower, upper].\n104\t *\n105\t * @param lower The lower bound of the range.\n106\t * @param upper The upper bound of the range.\n107\t *\n108\t * @return A random number within the specified range.\n109\t */\n110\tuint64_t randrange(uint64_t lower, uint64_t upper);\n111\t\n112\t/**\n113\t * @brief Generate a random number from a normal distribution.\n114\t *\n115\t * This function generates a random number from a normal distribution\n116\t * with the specified 